From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wu Yuwei <yuweiwu@pm.me>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:50:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vello_cpu: Add settings for the glyph atlas's pages and
 eviction

The glyph atlas's page size (4096), page limit (8) and eviction settings
were fixed. Before each render, the glyphs new to the atlas are drawn into a
scratch context of a page's size and composited onto their page, so the page
size is paid by every render that brings a new glyph, and `max_entry_age`
counts renders: a renderer that renders many small targets (a browser's
tiles) wants small pages and a longer age than a window's frames.

`Resources::with_glyph_atlas_settings` takes a `GlyphAtlasSettings`;
`Resources::new` keeps the defaults. `Resources::glyph_atlas_page_count`
tells how many pages the atlas has allocated.
---
 vello_cpu/src/lib.rs    |   4 ++
 vello_cpu/src/render.rs | 109 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 vello_cpu/src/text.rs   |  26 +++++-----
 3 files changed, 125 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vello_cpu/src/lib.rs b/vello_cpu/src/lib.rs
